hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19003","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, akhbarana Shuba from al-Aswad ibn Qays that he heard Jundub al-Bajali say: A woman said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I do not see but that your companion has been slow with you. He said: So this verse was revealed: Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you."
"19004","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar and Affan, both said: Thana Shuba from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Jundub who said: Something struck the finger of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Ibn Jaafar said: a stone - so it bled. So he said: Are you but a finger that has bled, and what you have met is in the path of Allah."
"19005","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shuba, akhbarani al-Aswad ibn Qays who said: I heard Jundub narrating that he witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he prayed then delivered the sermon and said: Whoever slaughtered before praying, let him repeat another in its place - and once he said another time: let him slaughter - and whoever had not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"19006","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana my father, akhbarana al-Jurayri from Abi Abd Allah al-Jushami, haddathana Jundub who said: A Bedouin came, made his mount kneel then hobbled it, then prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, he went to his mount, released its hobble, then mounted it, then called: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad and associate no one in our mercy. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you say this one is more astray or his camel? Did you not hear what he said? They said: Yes. He said: You have restricted a vast mercy of Allah. Indeed Allah created a hundred mercies, and Allah sent down one mercy by which creatures show affection to one another - its jinn and its men and its beasts - and with Him are ninety-nine. Do you say he is more astray or his camel?"
"19007","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Imran, meaning al-Qattan, who said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Jundub that a man was struck by a wound and was carried to his house, and his wound pained him, so he took an arrow from his quiver and stabbed with it his throat. They mentioned that with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said in what he narrates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic: He hastened to Me with himself."
"19008","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, haddathana Zuhayr from al-Aswad ibn Qays who said: I heard Jundub ibn Sufyan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ill and did not stand for two or three nights. A woman came to him and said: O Muhammad, I have not seen him near you for two or three nights. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers: Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you."
"19009","Haddathana Ubayda ibn Humayd, haddathani al-Aswad ibn Qays from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali then al-Alaqi that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Adha. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned and there was meat and the sacrifices of Adha, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that they had been slaughtered before he prayed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaughtered before we pray, let him slaughter another in its place, and whoever had not slaughtered until we prayed, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"19010","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Hammad ibn Salama from Ali ibn Zayd and Humayd from al-Hasan from Jundub that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the Fajr prayer is under the protection of Allah, so do not betray the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and let Him not seek you for anything of His protection."
"19011","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays who said: I heard Jundub say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ill and did not stand a night or two nights. A woman came and said: O Muhammad, I do not see your devil but that he has left you. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers: Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you."
"19012","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from al-Aswad ibn Qays al-Abdi who said: I heard Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Alaqi, a clan of Bajila, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Abd al-Rahman said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Adha to a people who had slaughtered or sacrificed, or a people who had not slaughtered or sacrificed - and he said: Whoever slaughtered or sacrificed before our prayer, let him repeat, and whoever did not slaughter or sacrifice, let him slaughter or sacrifice in the name of Allah."
"19013","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays who said: I heard Jundub al-Alaqi narrating that Jibril stayed away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was distressed. He said: So it was said to him. He said: So there was revealed: By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers: Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you. And I heard Jundub say: The finger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bled, so he said: Are you but a finger that has bled, and what you have met is in the path of Allah."
"19014","Haddathana Waki and Abd al-Rahman, both said: Haddathana Sufyan from Salama ibn Kuhayl who said: I heard Jundub say - Abd al-Rahman said: al-Bajali - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks repute, Allah will make him reputed; and whoever shows off, Allah will show off with him."
"19015","Haddathana Waki from Misar from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jundub al-Alaqi, he heard it from him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"19016","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Zaida from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr that he heard Jundub say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am your forerunner at the Hawd. Sufyan said: Al-farat is the one who goes ahead."
"19017","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from al-Aswad ibn Qays that he heard Jundub al-Bajali narrating that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he prayed then addressed and said: Whoever slaughtered before we pray, let him repeat another in its place - and perhaps he said: let him repeat another - and whoever not, let him slaughter upon the name of Allah, Most High."
"19018","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyayna from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he heard it from Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd. Sufyan said: Al-farat is the one who goes ahead."
"19019","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun and Ishaq ibn Yusuf, both said: Ana Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from al-Hasan from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever prays the Subh prayer is under the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so look, O son of Adam, let not Allah seek you for anything of His protection."
"19020","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Shuba from al-Aswad ibn Qays who said: I heard Jundub ibn Sufyan say: I witnessed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Eid on the day of Nahr, then he addressed and said: Whoever slaughtered before we pray, let him repeat his sacrifice, and whoever did not slaughter, let him slaughter upon the name of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"19021","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Abi Imran al-Jawni from Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran so long as your hearts are united upon it, and when you differ, then stand up. Meaning Abd al-Rahman - and Hammad ibn Zayd did not raise it."
